WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.449
The site director was boiling over with rage.

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:08.139
This was supposed to be a safe facility - one
where low-threat and well-behaved humanoid

00:00:08.139 --> 00:00:10.999
SCPs were kept with minimal security.

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:16.410
But if this kept up, these containment breaches
could easily bring the attention of SCP brass

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.180
- the last thing any of them wanted.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.090
“Can anyone explain?”

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.710
The director demanded, pausing to calm himself.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:27.060
“Why do we have so much trouble keeping
this subject safely contained?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.980
This is not the first containment breach!”

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.860
The security team looked at each other nervously.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.950
“Well, sir, nothing is ever certain.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.500
We’ve made sure everyone has the proper
security protocols in place, but SCPs are

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.620
always unpredictable - “

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.030
“It’s a little girl!”

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.840
The director slammed his fist on the table.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.810
“Look at these security protocols!

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:45.810
Stuffed animals!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.810
Playtime!

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.390
This girl is obviously not a threat - so what’s
going on here?”

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.309
The security heads exchanged another nervous
glance.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:58.350
“You’re right, sir - the specimen isn’t
the security threat here.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.010
It’s the researchers.”

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:05.750
SCP-2118 was secured by the Foundation with
both minimal apprehension as well as a smaller

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.780
team of personnel, after multiple reports
of her unique abilities were identified.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.290
She appears to be a normal child under ten
years of age, with orange hair and a long

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.450
scar on her right cheek.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.390
2118 claims that her scar is the result of
an assault by a stranger on the street.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:28.670
She communicated this via sign language, as
she rarely, if ever, vocalizes words.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:34.780
She is, however, capable of speech, and THAT
is where her unique abilities lie.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.740
SCP-2118 does not speak in her own voice,
and it is still unclear as to whether or not

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.830
she even possesses one.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.720
Her speech only activates in one situation
- in the presence of a parent who has lost

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.869
a child under the age of eighteen to death.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:57.369
Under this circumstance only will SCP-2118
begin to speak, but rarely in the same voice

00:01:57.369 --> 00:01:58.750
twice.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.890
Because SCP-2118’s voice isn’t her own.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:08.090
Automatically and involuntarily, 2118’s
voice pattern becomes that of the child who

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.870
died, speaking to their “parent” in a
way that reflects both the age and gender

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.170
of their deceased offspring.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:21.099
The voice that is heard is referred to as
SCP-2118-01 by the Foundation.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:26.760
SCP-2118 is aware of her speech and vocal
patterns as well as the psychological distress

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:34.620
they cause the parent, as she will use sign
language to apologize even as SCP-2118-01

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.810
continues speaking.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.599
But this isn’t the only disturbing part
of her abilities.

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:43.750
While at first the conversation can be generic,
most times the words and sounds coming out

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:49.379
of SCP-2118’s mouth reflect the final words
and sounds of the dead child.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.220
This not only includes disturbing pleas for
help, but can reflect the actual sounds of

00:02:54.220 --> 00:03:00.290
dying - mimicking the agony of drowning, disease,
or death by fire.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:05.970
SCP-2118 wasn’t necessarily a danger to
anyone - however, her presence could absolutely

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.500
pose a dangerous temptation.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.910
The director finished looking over the files.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:16.140
It seemed like everything had been handled
smoothly and by the books when SCP-2118 was

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.940
initially brought in - but along the way,
something had gone wrong.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.310
The case was being handled by one of his most
trusted researchers, Dr. Wu.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:30.760
As it became clear that SCP-2118 didn’t
talk normally, translators who could interpret

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.879
ASL were brought in for the first interview.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:39.550
Dr. Wu and site psychologist Dr. Lavoie welcomed
the strange little girl to the SCP facility.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:45.560
This interview provided the Foundation its
first intel on where SCP-2118 had come from.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.120
At first, the little girl was alarmed.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.760
She didn’t like being referred to by her
SCP number and insisted on her original name.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.920
She understood that she was in a science lab
of some sort, but thought she had been brought

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.450
there because she had done something wrong.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.440
She referenced a woman attacking her with
her purse at one point, and also claimed that

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.690
any time she spoke, people would get angry.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.690
But then she revealed something more disturbing.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.940
She knew why people got angry when she spoke
- from her mother.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.469
She had lived with her parent, and at some
point her mother had lost a baby - after the

00:04:19.469 --> 00:04:24.740
traumatic incident, every time 2118 spoke,
she spoke in the voice of the sibling she

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.169
had lost.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:31.689
This caused her mother to become angry, and
out of shame, provoked 2118 to glue her own

00:04:31.689 --> 00:04:33.779
mouth shut to prevent it from happening.

00:04:33.779 --> 00:04:38.960
Due to the glue being a little too strong,
it resulted in a visit to the hospital - something

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.800
she thought might happen again at the facility.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.060
But no one was sure if she was scared of it
- or hoping for it.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:50.669
More than anything, the little girl just didn’t
want people to stop talking to her.

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:55.610
The Foundation had a long way to go in understanding
SCP-2118’s abilities.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:05:01.129
Dr. Lavoie and Dr. Wu both seemed to have
a good rapport with the girl, and they were

00:05:01.129 --> 00:05:03.080
kept in charge of her case.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:07.960
Neither one had children, and could converse
with her without difficulty as long as a translator

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.139
was present.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:13.619
But to test her abilities, there would have
to be an experiment conducted involving someone

00:05:13.619 --> 00:05:15.930
who could actually activate them.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:21.800
And it just so happened that D-3498, a volatile
conscript working at the facility, had been

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.120
convicted of the murder of his wife - and
his daughter.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.449
BUT the experiment would prove to be more
than anyone was bargaining for.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:36.180
As soon as D-3498 was brought in, SCP-2118
became silent.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.509
After about thirty seconds, she signed an
apology for what was about to happen - and

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:43.159
then began screaming at the top of her lungs.

00:05:43.159 --> 00:05:48.469
She cried out for her father in an anguished
voice, all the while signing apologies.

00:05:48.469 --> 00:05:53.289
D-3498 became increasingly angry, demanding
to know what was going on.

00:05:53.289 --> 00:05:57.759
He struggled against his restraints and howled
obscenities as he listened to his daughter’s

00:05:57.759 --> 00:06:02.349
strangled pleas for help, begging, and ultimately,
her death rattle.

00:06:02.349 --> 00:06:07.429
Two agents, recorded as Agent M and Agent
C, were brought in to end the experiment and

00:06:07.429 --> 00:06:08.429
remove D-3498.

00:06:08.429 --> 00:06:12.599
And that’s when things took an unexpected
turn.

00:06:12.599 --> 00:06:19.110
While Agent C removed the D-class, Agent M
seemed oddly fixated on SCP-2118.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.529
The reason why became clear as soon as SCP-2118
opened her mouth.

00:06:24.529 --> 00:06:25.529
“Mama?”

00:06:25.529 --> 00:06:29.729
The voice had changed completely, to that
of a young boy several years older than the

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:31.289
D-class’ daughter.

00:06:31.289 --> 00:06:35.310
The boy seemed distraught, complaining of
being cold and scared and wanting to know

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.909
where his mother was.

00:06:36.909 --> 00:06:41.639
Agent M seemed frozen in place, and didn’t
answer Dr. Lavoie’s questions.

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:47.539
The experiment was quickly terminated, SCP-2118
was removed to her living quarters, and Agent

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:51.930
M was removed from duty with the case of a
possible missing or murdered child referred

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.899
to police authorities.

00:06:53.899 --> 00:06:59.529
SCP-2118 may have cracked a cold case - but
she also posed a dangerous temptation.

00:06:59.529 --> 00:07:04.029
It wouldn’t be long before the case had
its first security breach.

00:07:04.029 --> 00:07:09.229
Researcher Anselman conducted an interview
with SCP-2118 - despite not being assigned

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:10.479
to the case.

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:16.110
Anselman didn’t have access to the SCP’s
living quarters, so he watched SCP-2118 sleep

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.919
and then communicated with her through the
glass.

00:07:18.919 --> 00:07:24.279
The events were captured on facility cameras,
and showed that SCP-2118 was agitated from

00:07:24.279 --> 00:07:28.009
the start, knowing that Anselman was not supposed
to be there.

00:07:28.009 --> 00:07:31.009
And Anselman had an ulterior motive.

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:37.059
As soon as their conversation began, SCP-2118,
using sign language, asked Anselman why she

00:07:37.059 --> 00:07:39.050
was being made to do this.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:44.869
Soon afterwards, SCP-2118 started speaking
in the voice of a prepubescent boy that Anselman

00:07:44.869 --> 00:07:48.909
called Dewey - and who referred to Anselman
as dad.

00:07:48.909 --> 00:07:55.449
The boy was clearly agitated - as was SCP-2118
- and asked his father what happens after

00:07:55.449 --> 00:07:56.590
they die.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:02.099
Anselman became upset - wanting to hear answers
from his lost son, not questions.

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:07.110
SCP-2118 tried to warn him off, letting Anselman
know that he couldn’t actually communicate

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.619
with his son through her and she couldn’t
help him.

00:08:10.619 --> 00:08:16.469
But Anselman persisted, watching as SCP-2118
imitated the sounds of a boy gasping and taking

00:08:16.469 --> 00:08:22.659
his last breaths - consistent with a death
from illness, rather than accident or violence.

00:08:22.659 --> 00:08:26.939
All the while, SCP-2118 just watched sadly.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:31.319
The security breach was soon discovered, and
Researcher Anselman was removed and reprimanded

00:08:31.319 --> 00:08:35.030
for unauthorized testing with SCP-2118.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:41.000
But thanks to the researcher’s breach, the
Foundation did gain new knowledge of SCP-2118’s

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.649
abilities - namely that she couldn’t actually
channel the spirits of the dead.

00:08:45.649 --> 00:08:50.661
She was a mimic who could involuntarily duplicate
their last moments, but couldn’t provide

00:08:50.661 --> 00:08:55.879
any new information from them or answer questions
that they didn’t know in life - and she

00:08:55.879 --> 00:08:59.920
didn’t have any special knowledge of what
came after life.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.399
But her abilities did have one unique potential.

00:09:03.399 --> 00:09:08.360
By channeling the last moments of a deceased
child, she could possibly provide answers

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:13.040
for authorities as to their whereabouts or
their killer - as she had unexpectedly done

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:20.250
with Agent M. The problem was, this process
seemed to be deeply disturbing for SCP-2118,

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:25.889
who showed great emotional distress when forced
to channel a dead child and consistently apologized

00:09:25.889 --> 00:09:27.829
for the effect on the parents.

00:09:27.829 --> 00:09:30.889
Which left the Foundation in an ethical dilemma.

00:09:30.889 --> 00:09:31.889
“Sir?

00:09:31.889 --> 00:09:34.149
How do you want to proceed?”

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:36.560
The site director looked over the files.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:41.100
Clearly this couldn’t continue and something
needed to be done - but none of the security

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:45.709
breaches or other incidents had been SCP-2118’s
fault.

00:09:45.709 --> 00:09:50.370
She had been cooperative, despite the trauma
these tests seemed to cause her.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:56.080
To keep her safe, and to preserve her use
to the Foundation, things would need to change.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:02.209
“We could transfer SCP-2118 to a more secure
facility - but I’m not going to do that.

00:10:02.209 --> 00:10:06.839
Keep her cell furnished with all the things
a girl her age would want - it says here she

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:08.860
likes orcas and elephants.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:13.260
Take her outside to an enclosed play area
once a day, for about an hour - no more.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:18.000
But above all, make sure she’s always with
an attendant who can converse in sign language.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:22.660
She’s not to be around anyone who has had
children unless it’s necessary for testing.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.490
Convey these new parameters to Drs. Wu and
Lavoie, and make sure to increase security

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:30.270
around her quarters - as much for her protection
as anything else.”

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.800
The security team scurried off, happy to have
avoided the director’s wrath.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.459
The director turned back to the files.

00:10:36.459 --> 00:10:41.600
Yes, he had solved the problem for now, but
he would have to keep a closer eye on the

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.050
facility as a whole.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:48.209
The SCP foundation did close background checks
on its staff and on D-class personnel before

00:10:48.209 --> 00:10:54.029
bringing them in, but SCPs were unpredictable
- and you never knew what could make someone

00:10:54.029 --> 00:10:55.570
a security risk.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:59.260
How many employees working at the facility
had lost a child?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:03.980
How many, like the disgraced Researcher Anselman,
would do anything to hear their child’s

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:08.199
voice again - even if it was in the middle
of death?

00:11:08.199 --> 00:11:14.129
For another story of a seemingly harmless
child with unusual effects, check out “SCP-053

00:11:14.129 --> 00:11:16.730
- Young Girl”, or watch this video instead.

